IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, sections 118 and 119 -- DIRECTORS'
-- LIABILITY (for shares issued for property, for unlawful distributions and payments, and for employees'
-- wages). Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A cross-reference to
-- another piece is a plain input and says so. Money is a NUMBER of dollars.
-- Whether an act was "contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241" is a plain input: those sections
-- are out of range (pieces cb1, cb2 for s 124, cb4 and cb5).

§ `s 118 Directors' liability`

§§ `s 118(1) Directors' liability`

-- NOTHING: the director did not vote for or consent to such a resolution, or the share was issued for money, so
-- s 118(1) says nothing. The amount is the shortfall of the consideration received against the fair equivalent
-- of the money the corporation would have received had the share been issued for money on the date of the
-- resolution; no shortfall is no amount. Out of range: section 25 (piece cb1).
-- src:1399 | Directors’ liability
-- src:1400 | 118 (1) Directors of a corporation who vote for or consent to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25 for a consideration other than money are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable to the corporation to make good any amount by which the consideration received is less than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution.
@ref CBCA s 118(1) (src:1399-1400)
GIVEN `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share was issued for a consideration other than money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the consideration the corporation received in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount the director must make good within s 118(1)` MEANS
    IF     `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25`
       AND `the share was issued for a consideration other than money`
    THEN JUST (IF `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution`
                    GREATER THAN `the consideration the corporation received in dollars`
               THEN `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution`
                        MINUS `the consideration the corporation received in dollars`
               ELSE 0)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 118(6) No liability`

-- src:1417 | No liability
-- src:1418 | (6) A director who proves that the director did not know and could not reasonably have known that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money is not liable under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 118(6) (src:1417-1418)
GIVEN `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is not liable under subsection 118(1) within s 118(6)` MEANS
        `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money`
    AND `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it`

-- The two together: NOTHING where s 118(1) says nothing; JUST 0 where the defence succeeds.
-- src:1399 | Directors’ liability
-- src:1400 | 118 (1) Directors of a corporation who vote for or consent to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25 for a consideration other than money are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable to the corporation to make good any amount by which the consideration received is less than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution.
-- src:1417 | No liability
-- src:1418 | (6) A director who proves that the director did not know and could not reasonably have known that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money that the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money is not liable under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 118(1) s 118(6) (src:1399-1400 src:1417-1418)
GIVEN `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share was issued for a consideration other than money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the consideration the corporation received in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount the director owes after the defence within s 118(1) and (6)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount the director must make good within s 118(1)`
                 `the director voted for or consented to a resolution authorizing the issue of a share under section 25`
                 `the share was issued for a consideration other than money`
                 `the fair equivalent in dollars of the money the corporation would have received if the share had been issued for money on the date of the resolution`
                 `the consideration the corporation received in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        JUST (IF `the director is not liable under subsection 118(1) within s 118(6)`
                     `the director proves that the director did not know that the share was issued for a consideration less than the fair equivalent of the money`
                     `the director proves that the director could not reasonably have known it`
              THEN 0
              ELSE amount)

§§ `s 118(2) Further directors' liabilities`

DECLARE `Act authorized contrary to the Act under s 118(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a purchase, redemption or other acquisition of shares contrary to section 34, 35 or 36`
    `a commission contrary to section 41`
    `a payment of a dividend contrary to section 42`
    `a payment of an indemnity contrary to section 124`
    `a payment to a shareholder contrary to section 190 or 241`

-- NOTHING: the director did not vote for or consent to the resolution, or the resolution does not authorize an
-- act listed in paragraphs (a) to (e), or the act was not contrary to the section named, so s 118(2) says
-- nothing. The amount is what was distributed or paid and not otherwise recovered by the corporation.
-- src:1401 | Further directors’ liabilities
-- src:1402 | (2) Directors of a corporation who vote for or consent to a resolution authorizing any of the following are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable to restore to the corporation any amounts so distributed or paid and not otherwise recovered by the corporation:
-- src:1403 | (a) a purchase, redemption or other acquisition of shares contrary to section 34, 35 or 36;
-- src:1404 | (b) a commission contrary to section 41;
-- src:1405 | (c) a payment of a dividend contrary to section 42;
-- src:1406 | (d) a payment of an indemnity contrary to section 124; or
-- src:1407 | (e) a payment to a shareholder contrary to section 190 or 241.
@ref CBCA s 118(2) (src:1401-1407)
GIVEN `the director voted for or consented to the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e)` IS A MAYBE `Act authorized contrary to the Act under s 118(2)`
      `the act was contrary to the section named for it in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount so distributed or paid in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount otherwise recovered by the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount the directors must restore within s 118(2)` MEANS
    IF `the director voted for or consented to the resolution` AND `the act was contrary to the section named for it in that paragraph`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the act the resolution authorized, if it is one listed in paragraphs 118(2)(a) to (e)`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
          WHEN JUST act THEN JUST (IF `the amount so distributed or paid in dollars` GREATER THAN `the amount otherwise recovered by the corporation in dollars`
                                   THEN `the amount so distributed or paid in dollars` MINUS `the amount otherwise recovered by the corporation in dollars`
                                   ELSE 0))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 118(3) Contribution`

-- src:1408 | Contribution
-- src:1409 | (3) A director who has satisfied a judgment rendered under this section is entitled to contribution from the other directors who voted for or consented to the unlawful act on which the judgment was founded.
@ref CBCA s 118(3) (src:1408-1409)
GIVEN `the director has satisfied a judgment rendered under section 118` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other director voted for or consented to the unlawful act on which the judgment was founded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is entitled to contribution from the other director within s 118(3)` MEANS
        `the director has satisfied a judgment rendered under section 118`
    AND `the other director voted for or consented to the unlawful act on which the judgment was founded`

§§ `s 118(4) Recovery`

-- src:1410 | Recovery
-- src:1411 | (4) A director liable under subsection (2) is entitled to apply to a court for an order compelling a shareholder or other recipient to pay or deliver to the director any money or property that was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241.
@ref CBCA s 118(4) (src:1410-1411)
GIVEN `the director is liable under subsection 118(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director may apply to a court for an order compelling the recipient to pay or deliver within s 118(4)` MEANS
        `the director is liable under subsection 118(2)`
    AND `the money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241`

§§ `s 118(5) Order of court`

DECLARE `Order a court may make under s 118(5)` IS ONE OF
    `an order that a shareholder or other recipient pay or deliver to a director the money or property`
    `an order that the corporation return or issue shares to a person from whom it has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares`
    `any further order the court thinks fit`

-- The court may make the orders "if it is satisfied that it is equitable to do so", in connection with an
-- application under (4). (a) needs money or property paid or distributed contrary to the listed sections; (b)
-- needs a corporation that has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares from the person; (c) is open
-- whenever the court may act.
-- src:1412 | Order of court
-- src:1413 | (5) In connection with an application under subsection (4) a court may, if it is satisfied that it is equitable to do so,
-- src:1414 | (a) order a shareholder or other recipient to pay or deliver to a director any money or property that was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241;
-- src:1415 | (b) order a corporation to return or issue shares to a person from whom the corporation has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares; or
-- src:1416 | (c) make any further order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 118(5) (src:1412-1416)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 118(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is equitable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares from the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order a court may make under s 118(5)`
`the orders the court may make within s 118(5)` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made under subsection 118(4)` AND `the court is satisfied that it is equitable to do so`
    THEN (append (append (IF `money or property was paid or distributed to the shareholder or other recipient contrary to section 34, 35, 36, 41, 42, 124, 190 or 241`
                          THEN LIST `an order that a shareholder or other recipient pay or deliver to a director the money or property`
                          ELSE EMPTY)
                         (IF `the corporation has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares from the person`
                          THEN LIST `an order that the corporation return or issue shares to a person from whom it has purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired shares`
                          ELSE EMPTY))
                 (LIST `any further order the court thinks fit`))
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `s 118(7) Limitation`

-- src:1419 | Limitation
-- src:1420 | (7) An action to enforce a liability imposed by this section may not be commenced after two years from the date of the resolution authorizing the action complained of.
@ref CBCA s 118(7) (src:1419-1420)
GIVEN `the date of the resolution authorizing the action complained of` IS A DATE
      `the date the action to enforce the liability is commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the action to enforce the liability may be commenced within s 118(7)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`)
        `the date of the resolution authorizing the action complained of`
        `the date the action to enforce the liability is commenced`

§ `s 119 Liability of directors for wages`

§§ `s 119(1) Liability of directors for wages`

-- NOTHING: the director was not a director when the services were performed, so s 119(1) says nothing. The
-- debt is capped at six months' wages payable to the employee; how those six months' wages are counted is not
-- answered by the text (fork F-P10-9), so the figure is a plain input.
-- src:1421 | Liability of directors for wages
-- src:1422 | 119 (1) Directors of a corporation are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable to employees of the corporation for all debts not exceeding six months wages payable to each such employee for services performed for the corporation while they are such directors respectively.
@ref CBCA s 119(1) (src:1421-1422)
GIVEN `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount the director is liable to the employee for within s 119(1)` MEANS
    IF `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed`
    THEN JUST (IF `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars` GREATER THAN `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars`
               THEN `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars`
               ELSE `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 119(2) Conditions precedent to liability`

-- (a) sued within six months after the debt became due, and execution returned unsatisfied in whole or part.
-- "Within six months after" is counted in calendar months by the keel's convention (fork F-P10-10).
-- src:1423 | Conditions precedent to liability
-- src:1424 | (2) A director is not liable under subsection (1) unless
-- src:1425 | (a) the corporation has been sued for the debt within six months after it has become due and execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part;
@ref CBCA s 119(2) (src:1423-1425)
GIVEN `the date the debt became due` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the condition in paragraph 119(2)(a) is met within s 119(2)(a)` MEANS
        `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part`
    AND CONSIDER `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST sued THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`)
                                `the date the debt became due` sued

-- (b) liquidation and dissolution commenced, or dissolved, and a claim for the debt proved within six months
-- after the earlier of the date of commencement and the date of dissolution.
-- src:1423 | Conditions precedent to liability
-- src:1426 | (b) the corporation has commenced liquidation and dissolution proceedings or has been dissolved and a claim for the debt has been proved within six months after the earlier of the date of commencement of the liquidation and dissolution proceedings and the date of dissolution; or
@ref CBCA s 119(2) (src:1423 src:1426)
GIVEN `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the condition in paragraph 119(2)(b) is met within s 119(2)(b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier start`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST start THEN
        CONSIDER `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST proved THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) start proved
    WHERE
        `the earlier start` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been`
            WHEN JUST c THEN
                CONSIDER `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST c
                WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (IF c LESS THAN d THEN c ELSE d)

-- (c) an assignment or a bankruptcy order under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act, and a claim for the debt
-- proved within six months after the date of the assignment or order. Out of range: the Bankruptcy and
-- Insolvency Act.
-- src:1423 | Conditions precedent to liability
-- src:1427 | (c) the corporation has made an assignment or a bankruptcy order has been made against it under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and a claim for the debt has been proved within six months after the date of the assignment or bankruptcy order.
@ref CBCA s 119(2) (src:1423 src:1427)
GIVEN `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the condition in paragraph 119(2)(c) is met within s 119(2)(c)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST start THEN
        CONSIDER `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST proved THEN `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) start proved

-- src:1423 | Conditions precedent to liability
-- src:1424 | (2) A director is not liable under subsection (1) unless
-- src:1425 | (a) the corporation has been sued for the debt within six months after it has become due and execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part;
-- src:1426 | (b) the corporation has commenced liquidation and dissolution proceedings or has been dissolved and a claim for the debt has been proved within six months after the earlier of the date of commencement of the liquidation and dissolution proceedings and the date of dissolution; or
-- src:1427 | (c) the corporation has made an assignment or a bankruptcy order has been made against it under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and a claim for the debt has been proved within six months after the date of the assignment or bankruptcy order.
@ref CBCA s 119(2) (src:1423-1427)
GIVEN `the date the debt became due` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conditions precedent to the director's liability are met within s 119(2)` MEANS
        `the condition in paragraph 119(2)(a) is met within s 119(2)(a)`
            `the date the debt became due`
            `the date the corporation was sued for the debt, if it was`
            `execution has been returned unsatisfied in whole or in part`
    OR  `the condition in paragraph 119(2)(b) is met within s 119(2)(b)`
            `the date the liquidation and dissolution proceedings commenced, if they have`
            `the date the corporation was dissolved, if it has been`
            `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been`
    OR  `the condition in paragraph 119(2)(c) is met within s 119(2)(c)`
            `the date of the assignment or of the bankruptcy order, if there is one`
            `the date a claim for the debt was proved, if it has been`

§§ `s 119(3) Limitation`

-- "Sued for a debt while a director or within two years after ceasing to be a director": a director who has not
-- ceased may be sued; one who has ceased may be sued up to two years after the day they ceased.
-- src:1428 | Limitation
-- src:1429 | (3) A director, unless sued for a debt referred to in subsection (1) while a director or within two years after ceasing to be a director, is not liable under this section.
@ref CBCA s 119(3) (src:1428-1429)
GIVEN `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the director was sued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director was sued in time within s 119(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the director ceased to be a director, if they have`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN `the date the director was sued` AT MOST (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` ceased)

§§ `s 119(4) Amount due after execution`

-- Where execution has issued, the amount recoverable is what remains unsatisfied after execution. The figure of
-- s 119(1) still caps what a director owes, so the lesser of the two is recoverable (fork F-P10-11). NOTHING:
-- no execution has issued, so s 119(4) says nothing and s 119(1) governs.
-- src:1430 | Amount due after execution
-- src:1431 | (4) Where execution referred to in paragraph (2)(a) has issued, the amount recoverable from a director is the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution.
@ref CBCA s 119(4) (src:1430-1431)
GIVEN `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount recoverable from a director after execution within s 119(4)` MEANS
    IF `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued`
    THEN JUST `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1421 | Liability of directors for wages
-- src:1422 | 119 (1) Directors of a corporation are jointly and severally, or solidarily, liable to employees of the corporation for all debts not exceeding six months wages payable to each such employee for services performed for the corporation while they are such directors respectively.
-- src:1430 | Amount due after execution
-- src:1431 | (4) Where execution referred to in paragraph (2)(a) has issued, the amount recoverable from a director is the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution.
@ref CBCA s 119(1) s 119(4) (src:1421-1422 src:1430-1431)
GIVEN `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount recoverable from the director within s 119(1) and (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount the director is liable to the employee for within s 119(1)`
                 `the person was a director of the corporation while the services were performed`
                 `the debt payable to the employee for services performed for the corporation in dollars`
                 `six months wages payable to the employee in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST cap THEN
        CONSIDER `the amount recoverable from a director after execution within s 119(4)`
                     `execution referred to in paragraph 119(2)(a) has issued`
                     `the amount remaining unsatisfied after execution in dollars`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST cap
        WHEN JUST remaining THEN JUST (IF remaining LESS THAN cap THEN remaining ELSE cap)

§§ `s 119(5) Subrogation of director`

DECLARE `What a director who pays a debt under s 119 is entitled to` IS ONE OF
    `any priority that the employee would have been entitled to`
    `subrogation to the employee's rights as declared in the judgment`
    `an assignment of the judgment`

-- (a) in Quebec: subrogated to the employee's rights as declared in the judgment; (b) elsewhere in Canada:
-- entitled to an assignment of the judgment. Both only "if a judgment has been obtained".
-- src:1432 | Subrogation of director
-- src:1433 | (5) A director who pays a debt referred to in subsection (1) that is proved in liquidation and dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings is entitled to any priority that the employee would have been entitled to and, if a judgment has been obtained, the director is
-- src:1434 | (a) in Quebec, subrogated to the employee’s rights as declared in the judgment; and
-- src:1435 | (b) elsewhere in Canada, entitled to an assignment of the judgment.
@ref CBCA s 119(5) (src:1432-1435)
GIVEN `the director pays a debt referred to in subsection 119(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt is proved in liquidation and dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judgment has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director's claim arises in Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `What a director who pays a debt under s 119 is entitled to`
`what the paying director is entitled to within s 119(5)` MEANS
    IF `the director pays a debt referred to in subsection 119(1)` AND `the debt is proved in liquidation and dissolution or bankruptcy proceedings`
    THEN (append (LIST `any priority that the employee would have been entitled to`)
                 (IF `a judgment has been obtained`
                  THEN (IF `the director's claim arises in Quebec`
                        THEN LIST `subrogation to the employee's rights as declared in the judgment`
                        ELSE LIST `an assignment of the judgment`)
                  ELSE EMPTY))
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `s 119(6) Contribution`

-- src:1436 | Contribution
-- src:1437 | (6) A director who has satisfied a claim under this section is entitled to contribution from the other directors who were liable for the claim.
@ref CBCA s 119(6) (src:1436-1437)
GIVEN `the director has satisfied a claim under section 119` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other director was liable for the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director is entitled to contribution from the other director within s 119(6)` MEANS
        `the director has satisfied a claim under section 119`
    AND `the other director was liable for the claim`
